{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For every</b> (את). A sod: in the book of Genesis he did not mention [the name] until 'and they were completed,' there [using] for HaShem 'for Elohim' — it is the sod of the book of Ecclesiastes." "<b>And the meaning of 'upon every hidden thing'</b>: every deed that appears [to be] done will be brought to judgment according to what is hidden, and the matter is according to the intention of the heart, whether good or whether evil. And some say: even a thing that is hidden from you. And the first is more correct in my eyes." "And blessed is the one who knows the truth; from His kindness I ask to forgive my errors, and may my glory arouse until He makes known to me the path of life."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The comment is cryptic by design; 'did not mention' likely refers to a divine-name question, but the exact referent is uncertain. Translated hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:26.026876030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}